# Frontend environment template (safe to commit: contains NO real values).
#
# How to use:
#   1. Copy this file to frontend/.env.local (ignored by git).
#   2. Uncomment the lines you need and fill in the values there.
#
# IMPORTANT: the frontend only holds PUBLIC settings. Anything here can end
# up in the browser, where anyone can read it. Server secrets (database
# URLs, API keys such as AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY) NEVER go in the frontend -
# they live in backend/.env. Never give a secret the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix:
# Next.js copies NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables into the browser code.

# Address of our backend API (the Express app in backend/).
# Default when not set: http://127.0.0.1:4000
# It deliberately has NO NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix: only the Next.js server talks
# to the backend (from Server Components / Server Actions); the browser never
# does. Without the prefix, Next.js keeps this value on the server and never
# copies it into browser code.
# BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4000
